      "id": 1,
      "text": "Northgate Mall opened September 10, 1972, with Sears, McAlpin's, and Pogue's as its original anchors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northgate_Mall_(Ohio)"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1999 Dillard's bought McAlpin's, but that anchor closed in 2009 after a decade of operation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northgate_Mall_(Ohio)"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sears shut its Northgate location in November 2018, and Macy's followed in March 2020, leaving the mall without a traditional anchor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northgate_Mall_(Ohio)"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former Dillard's space was split into four big‑box stores in 2013: DSW, Marshalls, Michaels, and Ulta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northgate_Mall_(Ohio)"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A space that briefly hosted Famous Labels in 2010 became Burlington Coat Factory in 2013, marking a notable retail shift.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
